.TH GIT-UPDATE-REMOTE-BRANCHES 1 "2026-10-08" "Git Helpers" "git-helpers Manual"
.SH NAME
git-update-remote-branches \- push tracked branches to their configured remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git update-remote-branches
[\fB-n\fR | \fB--dry-run\fR]
[\fB--\fR [\fIpush-option\fR ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit-update-remote-branches\fR scans the local branches, finds the remote that
should receive pushes, and pushes any branch whose tracking state is out of sync.
It skips branches that have no remote tracking branch configured.
.PP
When run with \fB-n\fR or \fB--dry-run\fR, it reports which branches would be
pushed without updating the remote.
.PP
Any arguments after \fB--\fR are passed directly to \fBgit push\fR. If no push
arguments are provided, \fB--force-with-lease\fR is used.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git update-remote-branches
Push all local branches that are ahead or behind their tracked remote.
.TP
.B git update-remote-branches --dry-run
Report which branches would be pushed without sending anything to the remote.
.TP
.B git update-remote-branches -- --force-with-lease=main
Pass a custom push option through to \fBgit push\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-push (1)
